-- title:
--   Inertia at q acts by n on the reduction kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq p$, let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A_q$, and assume `ReductionInputsModL Aq p`: there is a system $r$ of places of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the modular function field of level $p$ which is a place reduction along $A_q$ relative to the residue map of $A_q$ and satisfies the condition `PrincipalGeneratedByIntegral`. Give $J =$ `JZero p`, the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of that function field, the `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[T_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$-module structure `heckeModuleBar p`. Then for all natural numbers $k, M$ and every function $n$ on $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ with values in $\mathbb{N}$ such that $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^{n(\sigma)}$ for every $\sigma$ and every $\zeta \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\zeta^{q^k} = 1$, the following holds: if $v \in J$ is annihilated by the ideal generated by the constant $q^k$ together with the $M$-th power of `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` (the preimage under `eisensteinEval p` of $q\mathbb{Z}$), and if $v$ reduces to $0$ under `reductionModL Aq p`, then $\sigma \cdot v = n(\sigma)\, v$ for every $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup of $A_q$.
--
--   This is the multiplicative-type statement of Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal: inside Eisenstein-bounded $q^k$-torsion, the kernel of reduction at $q$ is the part on which inertia at $q$ acts through the mod $q^k$ cyclotomic character, here recorded by the exponent function $n$. It feeds the counting arguments comparing the Hecke lattice quotient with the image of reduction mod $q$, such as [`ModularCurve.natCard_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_le_natCard_image_reductionModL_heckeTorsion_span_sup`](thm.html#ModularCurve.natCard_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_le_natCard_image_reductionModL_heckeTorsion_span_sup) and [`ModularCurve.exists_nsmul_generator_heckeTorsion_span_sup_of_inertia_smul_eisensteinMaximalIdeal_smul_eq_nsmul_of_ne_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_nsmul_generator_heckeTorsion_span_sup_of_inertia_smul_eisensteinMaximalIdeal_smul_eq_nsmul_of_ne_two).
